Dear all,

I have just updated to nimbleHMC version 0.2.1 (in linux) (and 0.2.0 in windows) and got a no assignation "error" wheras with the same code in previous versions of addHMC I did not.

To make it replicabvle I have checked I met the same problem with the simple code given with the help of addHMC and such is the case. Here is the code:

code <- nimbleCode({

    b0 ~ dnorm(0, 0.001)

    b1 ~ dnorm(0, 0.001)

    sigma ~ dunif(0, 10000)

    for(i in 1:N) {

        mu[i] <- b0 + b1 * x[i]

        y[i] ~ dnorm(mu[i], sd = sigma)

    }

})

N <- 10

constants <- list(N = N, x = 1:N)

data <- list(y = 1:N)

inits <- list(b0 = 1, b1 = 0.1, sigma = 1)

Rmodel <- nimbleModel(code, constants, data, inits, buildDerivs = TRUE)

## create MCMC configuration object

conf <- configureMCMC(Rmodel, nodes = NULL)

## add HMC sampler operating on all stochastic model nodes

nimbleHMC::addHMC(conf)

Rmcmc <- buildMCMC(conf)

Cmodel <- compileNimble(Rmodel)

Cmcmc <- compileNimble(Rmcmc, project = Rmodel)

samples <- runMCMC(Cmcmc)

I then get a warning after Rmcmc command:

[Warning] No samplers assigned for 3 nodes...

and the result is indeed stuck in the initial parameter values.

I meet this problem in both Windows and Linux, witj associated versions of Nimble of 1.1.0 in Linux and 1.0.1 in Windows.

I meet this problem with different models as well.

Do you figure out where my problem comes from?

I thank you very much in advance.

All the best,

Frédéric

